+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number). Each dish sold consumes one portion of its recipe per `qty`, with
+  the ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>` and the sale's instant. Tickets already
+  imported are skipped. Answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }` (`dishes`
+  counts dishes sold, the sum of `qty`). A bad row (`bad_request`) or an item
+  running out (`not_enough_stock_row`) imports nothing; the message names the
+  row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists, per item,
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`: theoretical use
+  from sales sold in those days (inclusive), actual use from every `consume`
+  movement in those days, and `difference` = actual - theoretical. Items where
+  both are zero are left out.
